{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CetceakU4FTPphVtE9zGk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Repo has an empty `intent/`, so this becomes `intent/0001-<slug>/intent.md`. Before I write it, a few analyst questions — the intent file should carry your words and observed facts, not my guesses.\n\n**Problem (observed facts)**\n1. \"A third of every call\" — is that a measured number (call logs, QA sampling, a support lead's estimate)? And roughly what volume: calls/week, average handle time?\n2. What exactly do customers ask? \"Where is my claim\" could be *which stage it's in*, *why it's stuck*, *when it'll pay out*, or *did you receive my document* — these are different features.\n\n**Scope**\n3. Which claim types are in scope — all of them, or one line of business first?\n4. Borderline items, in or out: showing the *reason* for a delay? Showing required documents / letting the customer upload? Notifications (email/SMS) when status changes, or portal-only?\n\n**Users and systems**\n5. Besides customers and support — do adjusters/claims handlers need to know that customers now see this? Anyone you haven't mentioned (compliance, brokers, agents)?\n6. Where does claim status actually live today (which system), and does the portal already talk to it?\n\n**Constraints**\n7. Anything that must hold — existing portal login only, no new PII exposed, regulatory rules about what you can tell a claimant mid-investigation, load limits on the claims system?\n\n**Success**\n8. Finish this sentence in your own words: \"This is done when …\" — and is there a number you'd check later (e.g. status calls drop from X to Y)?\n\nAnswer what you know; anything nobody can answer yet I'll record under Open questions with the name of who can."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":201,"cache_read_input_tokens":20621,"cache_creation"